Revision history for Perl extension CUDA-DriverAPI

{{$NEXT}}

    - First release to CPAN
    - Require Perl 5.40 and CUDA 12.0 or later, including NVRTC
    - Use the device primary context and the cuLibrary* API to load kernels
    - Add compile() to build CUDA C++ source at run time with NVRTC
    - Add buffer() returning CUDA::DriverAPI::Buffer, freed automatically
    - Add Buffer->write_array/read_array to convert nested arrays in C
    - write_array/read_array also take and return PDL ndarrays (optional
      dependency), copying their data without conversion
    - Add Buffer->fill (cuMemsetD8Async)
    - Add load() for compiled images and compute_capability()
    - Add `device` option to new()
    - run() launches asynchronously; add synchronize()
    - run() takes scalar kernel arguments by value ([i32 => 10], [f32 => 1.5], ...)
    - Cache loaded files and kernel functions per object
    - transfer_d2h($ptr [, $size]) returns the bytes
    - Bounds-check transfers against the allocation size
    - Report CUDA errors with their names and descriptions
    - Do not clone objects into ithreads (CLONE_SKIP)
    - destroy() releases everything even when a step fails
    - Fix out-of-bounds write when passing kernel arguments
    - run() checks the number and sizes of kernel arguments with drivers for
      CUDA 12.4 or later
    - Objects do nothing in a forked child: methods croak, and nothing is
      released through the parent's context
    - read_array croaks on dims such as [1e9, 0], which allocated a billion
      empty rows (empty arrays may have as many rows as the buffer has bytes,
      or 65536)
    - Load libcuda at run time, so the module builds and loads without an
      NVIDIA driver; new() then explains what is missing
    - Find the CUDA Toolkit without configuration (nvcc on PATH,
      /usr/local/cuda, /usr/local/cuda-X.Y, /opt/cuda, $CONDA_PREFIX, /usr);
      CUDA_HOME/CUDA_PATH pick a specific one. Without a toolkit, Build.PL
      stops with "OS unsupported"
    - compile() finds the toolkit headers (cuda_fp16.h, cuda/std/...) without
      options
    - compile() works with a toolkit outside the ld.so.conf paths (NVRTC finds
      libnvrtc-builtins through the module's DT_RPATH, which also takes
      precedence over LD_LIBRARY_PATH)
    - Tests use Test2::V0 and skip when no CUDA device is available
    - Add Perl::Critic author test
    - Replace Travis CI with GitHub Actions

0.01 2013-11-22 (not released to CPAN)

    - original version

